00:22:29,000 --> 00:22:40,000
given time, a surviving Neanderthal lineage wouldn't have arrived at complexity, sophistication, and self-awareness through its own root with its own character. They wouldn't be us.

173
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:50,000
They'd never be us. And that's precisely what would make them extraordinary. A mind shaped by different pressures. A body optimized for different conditions.

174
00:22:50,000 --> 00:22:57,000
A culture that grew from different seeds. Looking out at the same world through wider, darker eyes and finding it in whatever their equivalent of words

175
00:22:57,000 --> 00:23:05,000
would be just as bewildering, just as beautiful, and just as worth figuring out. The Neanderthalss are gone. We

176
00:23:05,000 --> 00:23:11,000
don't know exactly why, and we may never know for certain. What we do know is that they were here for 400,000 years.

177
00:23:11,000 --> 00:23:19,000
that they were more than we gave them credit for and that somewhere in the DNA of most people alive today, there's a

178
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:22,000
small quiet piece of them that made it through anyway. Not enough to hear their music. Not enough to read their script if they'd ever had one.
